{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21451 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside is implicated in the pathogenesis of SCCH-26 through a multi-step mechanism involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This compound acts as a target for multiple compounds, including WS-5995 B and a related epoxy compound, which in turn target SCCH-26. The evidence suggests that Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may modulate the proteasome pathway, potentially by interacting with the regulatory subunit 14, which is a key component of the proteasome complex. This interaction could disrupt the degradation of proteins, leading to cellular stress and possibly contributing to the malignant transformation of SCCH-26 cells. The presence of multiple targets in the pathway supports the hypothesis that Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside exerts its effects through a well-defined, mechanistically plausible route involving the proteasome. The integration of these findings underscores the potential of Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside as a therapeutic agent targeting the proteasome in the context of SCCH-26.",
